[WILD_PLAY_KEY]PFF_FE_KICKING_11
[PLAY_TYPE]KICKING
[ROLL]11
[SOURCE_TEXT]Kick is blocked and recovered by the defesne. Go to the Breakaway Chart to determine how many yds from the line of scrimmage the defense returns. If it's a kickoff resolve the normal way only the receiving player uses the breakaway chart to determine yardage gained. 
[SOURCE_REFERENCE]WildPlaysKicking.ods#Sheet1!A12:B12
[PROVENANCE_TYPE]OFFICIAL_PFF_BASE
[SCRIPT_LANGUAGE]GCE_WILD_PLAY
[SCRIPT_VERSION]0.1.1
[INTERPRETATION_STATUS]RULING_PENDING
[SCRIPT_STATUS]BLOCKED_BY_SOURCE_OR_RULE_RULING
[RULING_KEY]KICKING_WILD_PLAY_11_BLOCKED_KICK_RECOVERER_IDENTITY
[REQUIRED_WPSL_FEATURE_AFTER_RULING]BLOCKED_KICK
[REQUIRED_WPSL_FEATURE_AFTER_RULING]SPECIAL_TEAMS_RECOVERY
[REQUIRED_WPSL_FEATURE_AFTER_RULING]BREAKAWAY_FROM_LINE_OF_SCRIMMAGE
[REQUIRED_WPSL_FEATURE_AFTER_RULING]KICKOFF_RETURN_BREAKAWAY_OVERRIDE
[RULING_NOTE]The source specifies defensive recovery/Breakaway after a blocked punt or FG, but does not identify which defensive player recovered the ball even though Breakaway rating depends on player identity. The kickoff branch also replaces normal return yardage with Breakaway.
[DRAFT_SCRIPT_CONTENT_HASH_SHA256]cfd83264b3b69c9a9ce336c31aedaa21e0eb2bc98243f55481b96bcaec5a8254
[DRAFT_SCRIPT_BEGIN]
If KickType.IsKickoff {
    ResolveKickoff ReturnMode Breakaway NoAdjustments;
}
Else {
    BlockKick;
    RecoverBy {ReceivingPlayer};
    Invoke Breakaway From LineOfScrimmage;
}
[DRAFT_SCRIPT_END]
[WILD_PLAY_RESULT_END]

